From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 14:26:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: accept the 8-core J713 loaded 25G83 image

The 8-core M4 (J713, 13-inch MacBook Air) runs the same 25G83 G16 firmware
as the qualified 10-core image: build 2 of the 26.6.2 armfw_g16g.im4p.
iBoot patches the TEXT segment per device, so the loaded image differs
from the qualified hash only in the block iBoot fills in after the entropy
records (0x5c999-0x5d158: chip and revision records and a register
tunables table) plus one header word at 0x23d. The firmware code is
byte-identical, and the driver never reads that block: performance states
come from the ADT and the core mask from hardware.

Add the normalized SHA-256 of the 8-core loaded image as a second
FirmwareBuild so the driver accepts it. Measured on one 8-core J713 over
two boots, with the gpu-fw-text reservation dumped from the initramfs
(aligned 64-bit loads from /dev/mem) and normalized as the driver does.

Signed-off-by: Erik Bourget <erik@ebourget.net>
(cherry picked from commit 8eacef90ff8952b6fc75a85cb20abce488bcd4ed)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs
index 4ee9f5af9c..c68617064a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs
@@ -45,17 +45,32 @@ pub(crate) mod t8132 {
             version: 0x0a021100,
             counts: 0x0011010a,
         }],
-        firmware: &[FirmwareBuild {
-            name: "Apple GFX 25G83 (normalized loaded image)",
-            text_size: 0x60000,
-            data_size: 0x13c000,
-            marker: 0x5c8df,
-            text_sha256: [
-                0x5f, 0x65, 0xf6, 0x14, 0x58, 0x72, 0x54, 0x70, 0xb4, 0xb0, 0xc0, 0x20, 0x28, 0x47,
-                0x7b, 0xf2, 0xea, 0x57, 0x3a, 0xfb, 0x4e, 0x0c, 0x49, 0x6e, 0xf9, 0x95, 0xe9, 0x6a,
-                0xff, 0xb0, 0xd8, 0x6c,
-            ],
-        }],
+        firmware: &[
+            FirmwareBuild {
+                name: "Apple GFX 25G83 (normalized loaded image)",
+                text_size: 0x60000,
+                data_size: 0x13c000,
+                marker: 0x5c8df,
+                text_sha256: [
+                    0x5f, 0x65, 0xf6, 0x14, 0x58, 0x72, 0x54, 0x70, 0xb4, 0xb0, 0xc0, 0x20, 0x28,
+                    0x47, 0x7b, 0xf2, 0xea, 0x57, 0x3a, 0xfb, 0x4e, 0x0c, 0x49, 0x6e, 0xf9, 0x95,
+                    0xe9, 0x6a, 0xff, 0xb0, 0xd8, 0x6c,
+                ],
+            },
+            FirmwareBuild {
+                // The same 25G83 image (build 2 of armfw_g16g.im4p) as loaded by iBoot on an
+                // 8-core J713: only the block iBoot fills in after the entropy records differs.
+                name: "Apple GFX 25G83 (normalized loaded image, 8-core J713)",
+                text_size: 0x60000,
+                data_size: 0x13c000,
+                marker: 0x5c8df,
+                text_sha256: [
+                    0x3b, 0x36, 0x8e, 0xe4, 0x2d, 0xcc, 0xc6, 0x26, 0xe8, 0x49, 0x67, 0xff, 0x40,
+                    0x87, 0x64, 0x71, 0x0a, 0x64, 0xbf, 0xf1, 0x59, 0x4f, 0x3c, 0xfd, 0x2c, 0x6e,
+                    0x4d, 0x34, 0xd0, 0x65, 0x24, 0x8b,
+                ],
+            },
+        ],
     };
 }
 
